 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Lovely. Grabbing a quiet spot in the kitchen is lovely when everyone is there, so you' not right in the middle of things. A big whiteboard helps too, especially with that many. Then keep things moving, label each page with what time to come back to them, and write your name at the top of each. If you enjoy it and it' not too heavy, it adds a nice touch. Otherwise just serve one dish and keep it simple. Perfect. That gives you one main course to worry about. A big room is fine, as long as people can see each other and there are seats around the sides. Soft music in the kitchen helps too, so you' not constantly answering questions.",
